  "question": {
    "text": "Two tangents \\(P Q\\) and \\(P R\\) drawn to the circle \\(x^2+y^2-2 x-4 y-20=0\\) from point \\(P(16,7)\\). Ifthe centre of the circle is \\(C\\) then the area of quadrilateral \\(\\mathrm{PQCR}\\) is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "5a4fv",
      "text": "75 sq. unit",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "OKph6",
      "text": "73 sq. unit",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "p4ImU",
      "text": "72 sq. unit",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "5rD5M",
      "text": "74 sq. unit",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Area \\(\\mathrm{PQCR}=2~ \\triangle ~\\mathrm{PQC}=2 \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{~L} \\times r\\)\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/2MlwpK4A6CfMHiqk-ouZZSz-r8ZeW9skHwUpBdQRtt0.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nwhere \\(\\mathrm{L}=\\) length of tangent and \\(r=\\) radius of circle.\n\\(\\mathrm{L}=\\sqrt{\\mathrm{S}_1}=15 \\text { and } \\mathrm{r}=\\sqrt{1+4+20}=5\\)\nHence the required area \\(=75\\) sq. units.",
    "image": null
  },
